WEBVTT

00:02.470 --> 00:03.840
Damn it, Hyoma!

00:03.840 --> 00:05.330
Get back here, you asshole!

00:05.330 --> 00:08.010
Isn't it a little too early for yelling?

00:08.010 --> 00:09.190
H-Hey, Suzuri!

00:09.190 --> 00:11.180
Put a stop to this nonsense!

00:12.760 --> 00:13.950
It isn't nonsense.

00:14.420 --> 00:16.950
Nagatsuki-san was attacked. This is a fact.

00:17.790 --> 00:19.480
Therefore, as a protective measure,

00:19.480 --> 00:22.350
I must apply these around the mansion 
and its surrounding area!

00:22.350 --> 00:23.450
These talismans

00:25.170 --> 00:28.920
will immediately paralyze most tsukumogami 
entering their area of effect.

00:29.280 --> 00:31.300
They're a Saenome secret weapon!

00:31.300 --> 00:32.720
What are you, stupid?!

00:32.720 --> 00:35.880
That shit's powerful enough 
to give humans the shakes, too!

00:36.390 --> 00:37.390
Really?

00:37.390 --> 00:39.880
Besides, the mansion's safe.

00:39.880 --> 00:41.930
Kushige put a barrier up!

00:42.560 --> 00:44.170
No one mentioned that to me.

00:45.410 --> 00:46.690
But the truth is...

00:46.690 --> 00:47.750
What?!

00:48.230 --> 00:50.030
Did you already set them up outside?!

00:50.030 --> 00:51.680
I believed it was for the best!

00:51.680 --> 00:53.070
Take 'em down! Now!

00:53.520 --> 00:55.140
So much energy.

00:55.960 --> 01:01.080
Meanwhile, I'm way more worried 
about Kushige and Haori.

01:03.520 --> 01:06.340
Given who it was that issued the invitation...

01:07.120 --> 01:10.440
It's an open question whether 
they'll even make it back safely.

01:26.850 --> 01:34.610
<i>Malevolent Spirits</i>

02:48.020 --> 02:53.020
<b>Suspicions</b>

02:53.800 --> 02:55.510
Hey there, you two.

02:56.330 --> 02:57.900
Nice to see you.

02:57.900 --> 03:02.950
I feel like I'm a little too old 
for an invitation like this.

03:02.950 --> 03:06.760
It didn't feel that way the last time we met.

03:06.760 --> 03:08.200
How long has it been?

03:08.570 --> 03:11.150
Sixteen years, of course.

03:11.150 --> 03:15.210
But you look as young and dynamic 
as ever to me, Zohei-san.

03:15.210 --> 03:18.660
You do flatter me, Haori-san.

03:18.660 --> 03:22.890
And you're as laconic as ever, Kushige.

03:24.510 --> 03:28.110
I'd love to catch up,

03:28.110 --> 03:30.890
but we should save that for the after-party.

03:30.890 --> 03:31.960
That is...

03:32.590 --> 03:36.900
Assuming we're in any shape 
for it after we leave here.

03:40.100 --> 03:42.420
<i>It's my second time meeting him...</i>

03:43.180 --> 03:44.180
<i>Kai.</i>

03:45.280 --> 03:48.650
<i>Our last encounter was a brutal one.</i>

03:49.760 --> 03:51.910
<i>The first thing to look out for is</i>

03:51.910 --> 03:54.480
<i>a surprise attack to serve as a greeting.</i>

04:07.400 --> 04:09.130
Hey, now...

04:12.040 --> 04:13.430
You really need to...

04:14.600 --> 04:18.440
find a new way of saying hello already.

04:18.440 --> 04:21.570
Just being around you 
is exhausting like this.

04:22.030 --> 04:23.560
Do forgive me.

04:25.990 --> 04:30.490
Toying with visitors is one of my 
few pleasures in this existence.

04:36.880 --> 04:39.500
Welcome, Kunato.

04:40.500 --> 04:43.510
<b>Suit 
of 
Armor

"Kai"</b>

04:40.500 --> 04:43.510
<b>Kyoto's
 Three Great 
Tsukumogami</b>

04:44.010 --> 04:46.010
<b>— Itsuki —</b>

04:46.010 --> 04:49.680
And I'm glad to hear the Nagatsuki have 
been doing well since our last meeting.

04:51.380 --> 04:52.890
Did something happen then?

04:52.890 --> 04:53.930
Well...

04:53.930 --> 04:58.330
A few of our people came to offer 
our regards, but lost their tempers...

04:53.930 --> 05:02.190
<b>Our</b>

04:53.930 --> 05:02.190
<b>People</b>

04:58.730 --> 05:01.350
It turned into all-out war.

05:02.190 --> 05:05.100
It was effective at staving 
off boredom for me.

05:05.100 --> 05:07.510
I'd gladly take a rematch any day.

05:09.130 --> 05:15.020
And you chose <i>us</i> to stave off 
your boredom this time?

05:15.020 --> 05:16.580
Quite an honor.

05:16.580 --> 05:18.340
Now, now. Cheer up.

05:18.810 --> 05:22.140
In exchange for staying locked up in here,

05:22.140 --> 05:25.400
I'm allowed choose anyone to 
be my playmate at any time.

05:25.400 --> 05:29.910
It was the Saenome who offered 
these terms to me, wasn't it?

05:31.880 --> 05:35.770
I wish I could go back in time and 
pop those Saenomes in the nose!

05:37.760 --> 05:39.060
Absolutely agreed.

05:39.480 --> 05:42.410
<i>One of Kyoto's Three Great Tsukumogami...</i>

05:42.410 --> 05:44.490
<i>The suit of armor, Kai.</i>

05:45.360 --> 05:49.690
<i>Saenome documents say he first 
appeared early in the Edo Period...</i>

05:50.430 --> 05:54.010
<i>That he started out as a special 
exception to fight with them,</i>

05:54.010 --> 05:56.400
<i>but then, fearful of his power,</i>

05:56.400 --> 06:01.530
<i>they sealed him behind a barrier created by 
the shrine fence tsukumogami, Itsuki.</i>

06:02.740 --> 06:04.970
<i>One of the strongest.</i>

06:05.380 --> 06:09.830
I called you here because 
I heard some very interesting news...

06:10.510 --> 06:11.590
Itsuki.

06:12.640 --> 06:17.190
Kunato, they say your grandson has 
come to stay at the Nagatsuki household.

06:17.190 --> 06:19.140
Quite an interesting development.

06:19.140 --> 06:20.300
Tell me about it.

06:20.770 --> 06:23.340
I have food and drink available.

06:25.400 --> 06:29.450
Actually, I reserved lodging elsewhere.

06:29.450 --> 06:33.370
I'd prefer to leave here by six.

06:35.700 --> 06:37.660
Cancel the reservation.

06:38.790 --> 06:41.820
Your next few days belong to me.

06:42.290 --> 06:43.260
D—

06:43.260 --> 06:44.800
Days, plural?

06:47.120 --> 06:49.800
<i>What's truly terrifying about him...</i>

06:51.000 --> 06:54.220
<i>If he chooses you to pass the time with him,</i>

06:54.220 --> 06:58.280
<i>you could be held captive 
for an extended period of time.</i>

06:58.810 --> 07:02.390
I'd like to hear absolutely everything.

07:02.810 --> 07:03.750
Go on.

07:04.340 --> 07:06.340
<i>I knew it.</i>

07:08.490 --> 07:10.510
One, two, three...

07:11.210 --> 07:13.000
Just four left.

07:13.000 --> 07:15.910
A shame. I felt so sure they were necessary.

07:16.490 --> 07:19.770
They affect humans with 
a strong sixth sense, too!

07:19.770 --> 07:23.180
You're supposed to be protecting Botan, 
but you're just gonna upset her, man!

07:26.740 --> 07:28.180
<i>It is curious, though.</i>

07:28.670 --> 07:33.310
<i>A tsukumogami with a grudge against them 
attempted to take Nagatsuki-san hostage.</i>

07:34.160 --> 07:36.970
<i>This should have been a predictable 
consequence of their actions,</i>

07:37.560 --> 07:40.310
<i>yet they haven't resorted 
to measures like this.</i>

07:40.640 --> 07:44.900
<i>They must have great confidence 
in whatever defenses they have.</i>

07:47.840 --> 07:53.910
<i>Or is there something about Nagatsuki-san 
herself that makes protection unnecessary?</i>

07:54.600 --> 07:57.800
<i>It occurs to me that 
I know very little about her.</i>

08:02.360 --> 08:03.260
Yes.

08:04.530 --> 08:06.380
Only three remain now.

08:10.590 --> 08:12.890
What in the world...

08:14.290 --> 08:16.170
He sounds very interesting.

08:16.170 --> 08:17.850
Hyoma, his name was?

08:19.300 --> 08:20.850
I see...

08:20.850 --> 08:26.550
So you sent him to the Nagatsukis 
not for training, but for reformation.

08:27.980 --> 08:30.940
A man, heart frozen by hatred...

08:30.940 --> 08:34.500
Could the warmth of a simulated 
family free it from its icy prison?

08:33.570 --> 08:36.490
Hey! Don't sleep yet!

08:35.060 --> 08:40.490
In other words, can the deepest darkness 
of the human heart be expunged?

08:41.290 --> 08:43.540
Would that be your thesis?

08:44.190 --> 08:46.750
But you must be cautious.

08:47.280 --> 08:49.050
Regardless of your reasons,

08:49.050 --> 08:54.010
you've sent a third party to Nagatsuki Botan.

08:57.510 --> 09:01.270
<b>Don't make use of Nagatsuki Botan</b>

08:58.080 --> 09:01.270
"Don't make use of Nagatsuki Botan."

09:01.690 --> 09:05.890
You surely know the meaning 
of this unwritten law.

09:06.880 --> 09:11.940
The potential that lies within her could be 
a boon to either human or tsukumogami.

09:13.010 --> 09:17.260
She therefore cannot be allowed 
to take either side.

09:18.940 --> 09:24.910
"The head of the Saenome and 
Nagatsuki Botan's attendant tsukumogami

09:25.480 --> 09:30.700
have conspired to send a subordinate 
to woo her to their side..."

09:31.710 --> 09:34.870
Some may find that 
interpretation... convincing.

09:35.420 --> 09:38.310
If so, something may occur.

09:40.000 --> 09:41.000
Impossible.

09:41.430 --> 09:42.940
<i>It's been burned away.</i>

09:43.500 --> 09:48.040
<i>Which means the talisman activated, 
but its power was superceded.</i>

09:56.450 --> 10:00.660
I recognize the need to offer 
a full account to others...

10:01.080 --> 10:08.090
But I was afraid it might trigger 
a fight for a share of Botan's power.

10:10.070 --> 10:12.340
It's a matter that requires great patience.

10:12.970 --> 10:17.460
Though I believe others will 
already be jumping the gun...

10:25.880 --> 10:30.030
But at least it's entertaining, 
so it's a welcome turn for me.

10:32.310 --> 10:33.960
Hey, you.

10:34.780 --> 10:38.070
You know who put up that talisman?

10:40.730 --> 10:44.200
Or maybe... it was you?

10:45.110 --> 10:46.100
<i>They're...</i>

10:47.080 --> 10:48.360
<i>stronger than most.</i>

10:50.880 --> 10:52.080
Bingo?

10:57.670 --> 11:01.090
I was wondering why I suddenly felt sick.

11:01.740 --> 11:04.190
I happened upon a rather bizarre barrier.

11:04.190 --> 11:06.470
Is it crime prevention month 
and I simply forgot?

11:06.780 --> 11:11.100
<i>Actually, that was Hyoma 
running off half-cocked.</i>

11:11.100 --> 11:13.610
<i>We're in the process of taking 'em down now.</i>

11:14.120 --> 11:15.880
Glad to hear you found one.

11:15.880 --> 11:19.160
Give him a call and then help us out.

11:19.160 --> 11:21.290
The closer we come...

11:21.290 --> 11:23.240
Th-The tingling...

11:26.530 --> 11:28.830
I c-can't...

11:29.400 --> 11:31.020
take it... anymore.

11:35.440 --> 11:38.420
Goodness, what a slovenly display.

11:38.800 --> 11:40.920
We'll have to call a recess.

11:40.920 --> 11:41.780
Very well.

11:42.450 --> 11:43.430
By the way,

11:43.430 --> 11:45.680
shouldn't you have pressed them harder?

11:45.680 --> 11:47.310
That story they told...

11:47.630 --> 11:51.050
They're still hiding something from you.

11:52.190 --> 11:53.510
I suspected as much.

11:54.110 --> 11:58.460
It seems they'd already taken 
my warning into account.

11:59.660 --> 12:02.460
They welcomed a foreign presence 
into the Nagatsuki Household,

12:02.460 --> 12:05.320
even knowing the risk it would incur.

12:05.320 --> 12:07.880
But there's no need to rush.

12:08.570 --> 12:11.370
It's important to enjoy the process.

12:13.290 --> 12:16.250
Set up a network to watch for activity.

12:16.880 --> 12:21.850
If anything happens, 
I'd like a front-row seat.

12:27.540 --> 12:31.110
Haven't seen that sort of talisman 
around here before.

12:31.820 --> 12:37.270
Figured it had to have been 
stuck up there by some newcomer.

12:37.270 --> 12:40.900
We're looking for a guy named Kunato.

12:41.360 --> 12:44.180
We've got quite a few questions for the guy.

12:44.620 --> 12:45.910
So...

12:46.360 --> 12:48.410
Would that be you, then?

12:48.410 --> 12:51.680
<i>If they're aware of my presence,</i>

12:51.680 --> 12:54.900
<i>they must be monitoring movements 
around the Nagatsuki household.</i>

12:55.370 --> 12:58.430
<i>Which suggests they're allied 
with the tsukumogami</i>

12:58.430 --> 13:02.360
<i>with a grudge against the Nagatsuki ones.</i>

13:03.250 --> 13:05.880
Hey. You listening?

13:06.440 --> 13:07.820
<i>Their numbers are vast, then.</i>

13:08.400 --> 13:11.480
<i>They could prove a real 
threat to Nagatsuki-san.</i>

13:13.300 --> 13:14.580
Hey!

13:15.230 --> 13:17.430
I'm from the government office.

13:17.870 --> 13:21.570
I'm investigating reports of a 
curious new barrier in the area.

13:21.870 --> 13:23.690
I'm not the person you're seeking.

13:24.500 --> 13:25.570
Eh?

13:25.980 --> 13:29.560
Do you know anything about 
the person who put them up?

13:29.560 --> 13:31.030
"Kunato," you said?

13:32.120 --> 13:35.370
No... nothing in-depth.

13:35.370 --> 13:37.270
I see. Thank you.

13:39.380 --> 13:40.110
Farewell.

13:40.110 --> 13:42.600
I get it. The government office, huh?

13:42.600 --> 13:46.010
Sounds like tough work.

13:46.330 --> 13:50.260
Hang on! Normies don't know 
squat about barriers!

13:51.760 --> 13:53.890
<b>Kunato</b>

13:52.290 --> 13:53.620
The Kunato seal...

13:56.340 --> 13:58.060
Looks like I've got bingo after all!

14:07.940 --> 14:09.570
I'm taking you in alive!

14:09.570 --> 14:12.080
Tell me all about your comrades!

14:12.080 --> 14:13.880
Oh, no...

14:13.880 --> 14:15.080
Just kidding!

14:16.660 --> 14:18.580
You made two mistakes here.

14:18.880 --> 14:21.340
One was failing to land your strike on me.

14:21.840 --> 14:23.340
The other...

14:23.340 --> 14:26.500
was failing to finish off Uchiki-kun.

14:43.060 --> 14:46.060
Well? Cooled your head a bit?

14:51.940 --> 14:56.290
<i>That's right. He did save Botan earlier.</i>

14:57.800 --> 14:58.860
Hello?

14:58.860 --> 15:01.290
I found one of your talismans earlier.

15:01.720 --> 15:04.000
How many remain?

15:04.000 --> 15:06.800
If they're nearby, I'll try to find them.

15:07.300 --> 15:10.820
Yes, I'll gladly help clean up 
the mess you caused.

15:11.570 --> 15:14.050
That's about right, isn't it?

15:19.280 --> 15:21.810
Hello? I found one of your—

15:21.810 --> 15:24.620
<i>This is the voicemail service center.</i>

15:27.350 --> 15:28.870
I don't have a choice, then.

15:33.320 --> 15:34.650
Goodness me...

15:38.740 --> 15:41.830
Don't go too far now, Uchiki-kun.

15:42.640 --> 15:44.830
And you chill out too, buddy.

15:44.830 --> 15:48.460
We brought you here so we 
could have a little chat.

15:52.470 --> 15:54.720
You tried that one already.

15:52.470 --> 15:54.720
<b>Kunato</b>

15:54.720 --> 15:56.560
You know it won't work.

15:56.560 --> 15:59.930
All you did was seal another layer.

16:00.480 --> 16:02.600
You can't reach the core.

16:06.230 --> 16:09.050
Uchiki-kun?! No killing, now!

16:09.050 --> 16:11.290
We've still got to question him!

16:16.760 --> 16:19.820
I haven't been here long.

16:19.820 --> 16:23.400
I don't know the vulnerabilities of the 
tsukumogami hunters you hate so much.

16:24.670 --> 16:25.880
You're wasting your time!

16:26.170 --> 16:29.800
And even if I knew them, I'd never tell you!

16:32.010 --> 16:35.360
You're not really the listening type, are you?

16:35.360 --> 16:36.840
You're stupid, aren't you?

16:37.760 --> 16:39.710
Or are you playing dumb?

16:39.710 --> 16:43.020
Everything you say is so far off the money.

16:46.420 --> 16:49.500
We're asking about <i>you</i>.

16:49.500 --> 16:51.400
Don't lie, or you'll regret it.

16:52.310 --> 16:55.610
Entering the Nagatsuki household 
like a bolt from the blue...

16:56.720 --> 16:59.280
What exactly are you after?

17:00.150 --> 17:04.010
Do the Kunato seek the power 
that Nagatsuki Botan...

17:04.010 --> 17:06.290
that the yorimashi holds?

17:06.290 --> 17:09.290
Yorimashi? Power?

17:09.290 --> 17:13.040
The Nagatsuki tsukumogami, 
who are supposed to be neutral,

17:13.040 --> 17:15.060
have sold that power to the Kunato.

17:16.280 --> 17:17.450
Am I wrong?

17:18.800 --> 17:23.580
If it's true, it means 
they broke the rules first.

17:23.580 --> 17:28.510
It'll mean all-out war breaking out 
among us for Nagatsuki Botan.

17:28.510 --> 17:31.190
So? Why not tell me already?

17:34.740 --> 17:36.200
Interesting.

17:36.200 --> 17:38.900
I've never met tsukumogami like you before.

17:40.040 --> 17:42.750
You're using psychological warfare—

17:42.750 --> 17:45.870
lies designed to confuse me—
in order to catch me unawares.

17:47.330 --> 17:51.590
But I've been doing this 
too long to be deceived!

17:53.710 --> 17:56.860
You really don't like listening, do you?!

18:07.960 --> 18:11.270
I see no reason to heed 
the lies of tsukumogami.

18:11.860 --> 18:13.800
But I've learned one thing from this.

18:13.780 --> 18:17.900
<b>Kunato</b>

18:14.320 --> 18:17.900
You have your sights set on Nagatsuki-san.

18:17.900 --> 18:19.140
Which means...

18:20.180 --> 18:22.640
Seeing as you intend to 
attack an ordinary citizen,

18:22.640 --> 18:24.800
I'm duty-bound to seal you!

18:24.800 --> 18:27.040
And I will do my duty!

18:27.040 --> 18:29.370
An ordinary citizen?

18:29.370 --> 18:31.540
You're talking about Nagatsuki Botan?

18:34.560 --> 18:35.550
Eh?

18:36.080 --> 18:38.060
You seriously don't kno—

18:38.060 --> 18:42.930
He came here to learn from us 
as the next head of the Kunato.

18:43.310 --> 18:48.180
He's currently a guest under 
the guardianship of the Nagatsuki.

18:49.300 --> 18:51.740
If you stir up any more trouble 
with these false accusations,

18:51.740 --> 18:54.190
we're going to have a problem, Aogi.

18:55.300 --> 18:56.190
Yu...

18:56.750 --> 18:59.200
How did you know we were here?

19:04.270 --> 19:07.610
I followed the scraps 
of burned-out talismans...

19:07.610 --> 19:10.080
And look what a troublesome scene I've found.

19:10.630 --> 19:11.990
But Aogi...

19:13.040 --> 19:16.870
If you've learned what you need to know, 
you should probably leave.

19:17.810 --> 19:19.220
Shouldn't you?

19:23.800 --> 19:26.090
Yeah, I'm getting nowhere here.

19:26.090 --> 19:30.200
Doesn't look like he'll 
give up anything useful.

19:31.230 --> 19:32.560
You won't escape!

19:34.440 --> 19:36.170
Didn't I tell you?

19:36.170 --> 19:38.440
Any more escalation and we'll have a problem.

19:38.440 --> 19:42.970
Their methods may be extreme, 
but their actions are permitted.

19:48.600 --> 19:49.800
Special exceptions...

19:49.800 --> 19:51.580
The twelve-layer robe, Uchiki,

19:50.080 --> 19:54.080
<b>War Fan
Aogi</b>

19:50.080 --> 19:54.080
<b>Twelve-Layer Robe
 Uchiki</b>

19:51.580 --> 19:53.180
and the war fan, Aogi.

19:54.880 --> 19:58.920
Their primary duties are internal 
investigations and intelligence gathering.

20:00.480 --> 20:03.340
I'm forced to wonder who hired them today.

20:03.340 --> 20:05.220
Correct.

20:05.690 --> 20:09.480
It seems looking for ulterior motives 
in him is a waste of time.

20:10.190 --> 20:15.630
For now, I'll have to buy your explanation—
that it's for training—and withdraw.

20:15.630 --> 20:16.360
Besides...

20:18.080 --> 20:22.020
Someone's been watching us for a while.

20:25.410 --> 20:27.280
I'll admit I went too far,

20:27.280 --> 20:28.760
but I won't apologize.

20:28.760 --> 20:30.420
This is the job, after all.

20:31.010 --> 20:31.900
Although...

20:32.570 --> 20:36.680
I've received requests to investigate what 
Kunato is doing at the Nagatsuki Household

20:36.680 --> 20:39.800
from both humans and tsukumogami.

20:39.800 --> 20:42.460
There are many eyes on you.

20:42.460 --> 20:44.660
You'd better watch your backs.

20:46.840 --> 20:48.300
Honestly...

20:48.300 --> 20:49.990
It's constant trouble.

20:52.080 --> 20:54.080
<i>I could have beaten them.</i>

20:54.080 --> 20:57.260
<i>I'd figured out how to beat Uchiki,</i>

20:57.260 --> 20:59.790
<i>and I was an equally able fighter.</i>

20:59.790 --> 21:00.940
<i>Two against one?</i>

21:00.940 --> 21:02.490
<i>Not an issue.</i>

21:02.490 --> 21:05.480
<i>Once one was locked down, 
I could have easily beat the other.</i>

21:05.960 --> 21:08.970
<i>Had the fight continued, I would have won.</i>

21:08.970 --> 21:09.820
Ow!

21:09.820 --> 21:10.830
Calm down.

21:13.080 --> 21:14.940
You're clearly in bad shape.

21:14.940 --> 21:18.080
I'll retrieve the other talismans.

